            {
              "text": "When selecting a Microsoft Power Platform partner in Melbourne, the right choice depends on whether you need a **workplace enablement and governance partner**, a **deep Dynamics 365/enterprise integration**, or a **large-scale enterprise transformation**.\n\nThe following shortlist highlights reputable Microsoft consulting partners with established delivery teams and strong presences in Melbourne.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Engage Squared\n* **Best for:** Workplace Automation, Adoption & Power Platform Governance (CoE)\n* **Location:** Headquartered in Melbourne\n* **Overview:** A multi-award-winning Microsoft partner (past Microsoft Australia Partner of the Year), Engage Squared specializes heavily in Microsoft 365, Copilot, and the Power Platform ecosystem. \n* **Why them:** \n  * They are widely regarded for combining technical development with **change management and human-centred design**.\n  * Ideal for establishing a **Power Platform Center of Excellence (CoE)**, setting up citizen-developer guardrails, preventing \"sprawl,\" and digitising operational workflows (e.g., field-worker forms, internal request portals).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Barhead Solutions\n* **Best for:** Complex Line-of-Business Apps, Dataverse & Dynamics 365 Alignment\n* **Location:** Melbourne office (Docklands/CBD) & Sydney\n* **Overview:** Barhead is a recognized tier-1 specialist in Microsoft Business Applications and Power Platform across Australia.\n* **Why them:**\n  * If your Power Platform initiative involves connecting directly to or building around **Dynamics 365 (CRM/ERP), Common Data Service / Dataverse**, or advanced custom connectors, Barhead is a top-tier choice.\n  * They run regular Microsoft *“App in a Day”* training workshops and have extensive experience delivering regulated, secure apps for banking, non-profit, and public-sector clients.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Rapid Circle\n* **Best for:** End-to-End Modern Workplace Modernisation & Legacy App Replacement\n* **Location:** Melbourne office (along with Brisbane and Sydney)\n* **Overview:** A Microsoft Cloud Solutions Partner with deep roots in modern workplace solutions, Rapid Circle expanded its Australian capability significantly in recent years.\n* **Why them:**\n  * Excellent for replacing antiquated setups (legacy SharePoint InfoPath forms, Lotus Notes, unwieldy Excel workflows) with modern Power Apps, Power Automate, and Copilot Studio agents.\n  * Strong technical discipline around secure architecture, Microsoft Teams integration, and identity management.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Professional Advantage\n* **Best for:** Mid-Market Operations, ERP Integration & Power BI Reporting\n* **Location:** Melbourne office (along with Sydney and Brisbane)\n* **Overview:** In operation for over three decades, Professional Advantage is one of the most established Microsoft mid-market solutions providers in Australia.\n* **Why them:**\n  * Strong for businesses looking to tie Power Apps and Power Automate directly into core back-office systems like **Dynamics 365 Business Central**.\n  * Proven delivery record in turning disparate business data into unified dashboards using **Power BI** alongside automated transactional workflows.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Avanade Australia\n* **Best for:** Tier-1 Enterprise, Mission-Critical Scale & Regulated Sectors\n* **Location:** Melbourne CBD\n* **Overview:** The joint venture between Accenture and Microsoft, Avanade is the heavyweight global systems integrator for Microsoft technologies.\n* **Why them:**\n  * If you operate in government, tier-1 banking, healthcare, or major infrastructure, and require multi-environment governance, dedicated enterprise ALM (Application Lifecycle Management) pipelines, and strict SOC/ISO compliance, Avanade has scale that boutique firms cannot match.\n  * Ideal for large programmes where Power Platform forms only one part of an extensive Azure and AI transformation.\n\n---\n\n### Key Questions to Ask When Selecting a Consultant\n\nBefore engaging any partner, ensure you evaluate:\n1. **Governance & ALM (DevOps):** Do they build apps in default environments, or do they establish formal Dev/Test/Prod pipelines and data loss prevention (DLP) policies?\n2. **Licensing Advisory:** Power Platform licensing (per-app vs per-user vs Dataverse capacity vs PAYG Azure meters) can scale unpredictably. A good partner will help architect solutions to avoid unnecessary licensing costs.\n3. **Copilot / AI Integration:** Ask how they leverage **Copilot Studio** and AI Builder natively within Power Automate/Power Apps.",
